>Bipartite Graph Validation</h1></header><div class=3D"style-module-scss-mo=
dule__ubvNPq__problemDescription"><p>Given an undirected graph, determine i=
f it's bipartite. A graph is bipartite if the nodes can be colored in one o=
f two colors, so that <strong>no two adjacent nodes are the same color</str=
ong>.</p><p>The input is presented as an adjacency list, where <code>graph[=
i]</code> is a list of all nodes adjacent to node <code>i</code>.</p><h4 id=
=3D"example">Example:</h4><figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display:flex=
;justify-content:center"><img alt=3D"Image represents a graph, specifically=
 a cycle graph of five nodes (vertices) arranged in a circular pattern.  No=
